.TH DOTTY 1 "" "Dotty" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dotty \- GPU\-accelerated terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
dotty [\-\-working\-directory DIR|\-d DIR] [\-\-shell PATH] [\-\-] [COMMAND [ARG...]]
dotty \-\-help|\-h
dotty \-\-version
dotty +ACTION [ARG...]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dotty opens a terminal window running the user's shell, or COMMAND with its exact arguments when one is given.
Arguments that start with \fB+\fR run an action that prints and exits without opening a window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Show version and exit
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-working\-directory\fR \fIDIR\fR
Start in DIR
.TP
\fB\-\-shell\fR \fIPATH\fR
Start PATH as the interactive shell
.TP
\fB\-\-\fR
End Dotty options; run COMMAND with exact arguments
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
\fB+explain\-config\fR [OPTION]
List every config option, or document OPTION (JSON path or Lua key, e.g. font.size)
.TP
\fB+init\-config\fR [\-\-force]
Write a commented starter config.json; \-\-force replaces an existing file
.TP
\fB+show\-config\fR [\-\-default]
Print the effective config.json settings as JSON, or the built\-in defaults with \-\-default
.TP
\fB+validate\-config\fR
Check config.json and config.lua; exit 1 and print file:line errors when something is wrong
.TP
\fB+list\-themes\fR
List built\-in and user theme names
.TP
\fB+diagnose\fR [\-\-gl]
Print version, platform, paths, config status and helper locations; \-\-gl also probes OpenGL
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from \fIconfig.json\fR (and \fIconfig.lua\fR) in the configuration directory:
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dotty\fR, or \fI~/.config/dotty\fR. \fBdotty +explain\-config\fR \fIOPTION\fR prints the default and allowed values of one option.
The options are listed by JSON path, followed by the Lua key under \fBdotty.config\fR.
.TP
\fBbell.attention\fR (boolean; Lua \fBbell.attention\fR)
On a terminal bell, request window attention (taskbar flash, dock bounce, urgency hint) while the window is not focused.
.TP
\fBbell.audible\fR (boolean; Lua \fBbell.audible\fR)
Play a sound on a terminal bell. Accepted but not yet implemented on any platform: no sound is played.
.TP
\fBbell.visual\fR (boolean; Lua \fBbell.visual\fR)
On a terminal bell, briefly flash the window contents (about 150 ms fade).
.TP
\fBclipboard.allowOsc52Write\fR (boolean; Lua \fBclipboard.allow_osc52_write\fR)
Let terminal applications write to the system clipboard with OSC 52; a Lua clipboard_write hook can veto but never grant.
.TP
\fBclipboard.bracketedPasteIsSafe\fR (boolean; Lua \fBclipboard.bracketed_paste_is_safe\fR)
When the application enabled bracketed paste, multi\-line text alone does not need confirmation; control characters and end markers still do.
.TP
\fBclipboard.confirmPaste\fR (boolean; Lua \fBclipboard.confirm_paste\fR)
Ask before pasting text that contains line breaks, control characters, or a bracketed\-paste end marker.
.TP
\fBclipboard.osc52Read\fR (string; Lua \fBclipboard.osc52_read\fR)
Policy for OSC 52 clipboard read requests; case\-insensitive, any other value is treated as deny. 'allow' lets any program that prints to the terminal read your clipboard. One of: deny, ask, allow.
.TP
\fBclipboard.osc52ReadLimitBytes\fR (integer; Lua \fBclipboard.osc52_read_limit_bytes\fR)
Largest clipboard (UTF\-8 bytes) an OSC 52 read may return; larger clipboards are dropped without a reply. Clamped to 1 through 8388608.
.TP
\fBcursor.blink\fR (boolean; Lua \fBcursor.blink\fR)
Default cursor blinking, used until the application selects a style with DECSCUSR; blinking stops while the window is unfocused.
.TP
\fBcursor.blinkIntervalMs\fR (integer; Lua \fBcursor.blink_interval_ms\fR)
Blink interval in milliseconds for the cursor and SGR 5/6 blinking text; values below 100 are raised to 100.
.TP
\fBcursor.shape\fR (string; Lua \fBcursor.shape\fR)
Default cursor shape, used until the application selects one with DECSCUSR (CSI Ps SP q); DECSCUSR 0, DECSTR and RIS return to it. One of: Block, Beam, Underline.
.TP
\fBcursor.text\fR (string; Lua \fBcursor.text\fR)
Text colour inside a block cursor: 'auto' uses the cell background (the cell foreground when the background matches the cursor), 'cell\-foreground' keeps the text colour. One of: auto, cell\-foreground.
.TP
\fBcursor.unfocusedStyle\fR (string; Lua \fBcursor.unfocused_style\fR)
Cursor while the window is unfocused: an outline of the cursor cell ('hollow'), the focused shape ('same'), or none ('hidden'). One of: hollow, same, hidden.
.TP
\fBfont.adjustCellHeight\fR (string; Lua \fBfont.adjust_cell_height\fR)
Cell height adjustment: signed logical pixels ('2') or percent ('\-5%'), at most 100 either way; the change is split above and below the text.
.TP
\fBfont.adjustCellWidth\fR (string; Lua \fBfont.adjust_cell_width\fR)
Cell width adjustment: signed logical pixels ('1', '\-0.5') or percent ('10%'), at most 100 either way; empty or malformed keeps the measured width.
.TP
\fBfont.boldFamily\fR (string; Lua \fBfont.bold_family\fR)
Comma\-separated families for bold text in the primary font; empty uses the primary family's bold face, synthetic bold when it has none.
.TP
\fBfont.boldItalicFamily\fR (string; Lua \fBfont.bold_italic_family\fR)
Comma\-separated families for bold italic text in the primary font; empty uses the primary family's bold italic face, synthesized when missing.
.TP
\fBfont.builtinGlyphs\fR (boolean; Lua \fBfont.builtin_glyphs\fR)
Draw box drawing (U+2500\-257F), block elements (U+2580\-259F), braille (U+2800\-28FF), sextants (U+1FB00\-1FB3B), octants (U+1CD00\-1CDE5) and Powerline (U+E0B0\-E0BF) as pixel\-exact built\-in sprites instead of font glyphs.
.TP
\fBfont.faintOpacity\fR (number; Lua \fBfont.faint_opacity\fR)
Share of its own colour that faint (SGR 2) text keeps when mixed toward the cell background; clamped to 0\-1, non\-finite values use 0.5.
.TP
\fBfont.family\fR (string; Lua \fBfont.family\fR)
Comma\-separated font family names; the first installed family wins.
.TP
\fBfont.features\fR (string[]; Lua \fBfont.features\fR)
OpenType feature settings for shaping: '+calt', '\-liga', 'ss01', 'cv01=2'; a tag is four letters or digits, later settings of a tag win, invalid entries are ignored.
.TP
\fBfont.italicFamily\fR (string; Lua \fBfont.italic_family\fR)
Comma\-separated families for italic text in the primary font; empty uses the primary family's italic face, synthetic slant when it has none.
.TP
\fBfont.lineHeight\fR (number; Lua \fBfont.line_height\fR)
Line\-height multiplier; values below 0.1 are clamped.
.TP
\fBfont.size\fR (number; Lua \fBfont.size\fR)
Font size in points (pixels = points x 96/72 x display scale; default 11.25 = 15 px at 100 %); clamped to 1\-512, non\-finite values use the default.
.TP
\fBfont.symbolMap\fR (string[]; Lua \fBfont.symbol_map\fR)
Per\-range font overrides, one per entry: 'U+2500\-U+257F: Preferred Font, Fallback Font'; the first installed family containing the glyph wins.
.TP
\fBfont.weight\fR (string; Lua \fBfont.weight\fR)
Weight of regular text: thin, extralight, light, regular, medium, semibold, bold, extrabold, black or a number 1\-1000; bold text uses 700 (900 from semibold up).
.TP
\fBgraphics.allowFileTransfer\fR (boolean; Lua \fBgraphics.allow_file_transfer\fR)
Let graphics clients transmit images by reading a regular file path (t=f).
.TP
\fBgraphics.allowSharedMemory\fR (boolean; Lua \fBgraphics.allow_shared_memory\fR)
Let graphics clients transmit images through a POSIX shared\-memory object (t=s).
.TP
\fBgraphics.allowTempFileTransfer\fR (boolean; Lua \fBgraphics.allow_temp_file_transfer\fR)
Let graphics clients transmit images through a temporary file that the terminal deletes after reading (t=t).
.TP
\fBgraphics.imageStorageLimitMiB\fR (integer; Lua \fBgraphics.image_storage_limit_mib\fR)
Per\-session budget for stored image pixels, in MiB. Non\-positive values fall back to the default; clamped to at most 4096.
.TP
\fBgraphics.kittyProtocol\fR (boolean; Lua \fBgraphics.kitty_protocol\fR)
Enable the Kitty graphics protocol (APC G): programs may transmit, place and delete inline images. When false the sequences are ignored.
.TP
\fBgraphics.maxPayloadMiB\fR (integer; Lua \fBgraphics.max_payload_mib\fR)
Largest single image transmission accepted, in MiB. Non\-positive values fall back to the default; clamped to at most 1024.
.TP
\fBgraphics.windowsPassthrough\fR (boolean; Lua \fBgraphics.windows_passthrough\fR)
Windows only, experimental: create the ConPTY in passthrough mode so graphics sequences are not dropped. May change how ConPTY forwards VT output; verify before enabling. Ignored on other platforms.
.TP
\fBhyperlinks.allowedSchemes\fR (string[]; Lua \fBhyperlinks.allowed_schemes\fR)
URI schemes that may be opened (case\-insensitive); hard\-blocked schemes cannot be enabled by listing them.
.TP
\fBhyperlinks.confirm\fR (string; Lua \fBhyperlinks.confirm\fR)
When to ask before opening a link; unknown values mean risky. Hard\-blocked schemes are refused in every mode. One of: risky, always, never.
.TP
\fBhyperlinks.osc8\fR (boolean; Lua \fBhyperlinks.osc8\fR)
Honor OSC 8 explicit hyperlinks; when false they are ignored at ingest. Detected plain URLs are unaffected.
.TP
\fBkeybindings\fR (map; Lua \fBkeybindings\fR)
Map of chord ('ctrl+shift+t', 'cmd+k', 'physical:ctrl+shift+c') to an action name such as new_tab, copy or send_text:\ex01; 'none' unbinds a chord. Entries are added to the built\-in bindings, which are not part of this default; rejected entries are logged and listed by +validate\-config.
.TP
\fBkeyboard.leftAlt\fR (string; Lua \fBkeyboard.left_alt\fR)
Left Alt/Option: 'meta' sends Alt chords as ESC\-prefixed input and matches alt+ bindings, 'compose' types the character the layout composes (Option on macOS), 'auto' is meta on Linux/Windows and compose on macOS. Case\-insensitive; unknown values mean auto. One of: auto, meta, compose.
.TP
\fBkeyboard.rightAlt\fR (string; Lua \fBkeyboard.right_alt\fR)
Right Alt/Option (AltGr): 'auto' is compose on Linux/Windows when the layout has AltGr and meta when it does not, and compose on macOS; 'meta' and 'compose' force one behavior. Case\-insensitive; unknown values mean auto. One of: auto, meta, compose.
.TP
\fBmouse.alternateScroll\fR (string; Lua \fBmouse.alternate_scroll\fR)
\&'auto' sends cursor up/down for the wheel while the alternate screen is shown, no mouse reporting is active and the application has not reset mode 1007 (less, man, editors without mouse support); 'off' never does. Unknown values mean auto. One of: auto, off.
.TP
\fBmouse.copyOnSelect\fR (string; Lua \fBmouse.copy_on_select\fR)
Where a finished local selection is copied automatically; it does not clear the selection and does not affect middle\-click. Case\-insensitive; the legacy spellings "true" (primary on Linux, clipboard elsewhere) and "false" (none) are also accepted as strings, and unknown values mean none. One of: none, primary, clipboard, both.
.TP
\fBmouse.middleClickAction\fR (string; Lua \fBmouse.middle_click_action\fR)
What a middle\-click in a pane does when the application is not capturing the mouse: paste the primary selection, paste the clipboard, or nothing. Unknown values mean clipboard\-paste. One of: primary\-paste, clipboard\-paste, ignore.
.TP
\fBmouse.reportBypassModifier\fR (string; Lua \fBmouse.report_bypass_modifier\fR)
Modifier that, while held, keeps clicks, drags and the wheel local (selection, scrollback) when an application tracks the mouse; 'none' always reports. Unknown values mean shift. One of: shift, ctrl, alt, super, none.
.TP
\fBmouse.scrollMultiplier\fR (number; Lua \fBmouse.scroll_multiplier\fR)
Lines scrolled per wheel notch, for local scrollback and for alternate\-scroll cursor keys; fractional touchpad deltas accumulate until a whole line. Applications that track the mouse get one wheel report per notch regardless. Clamped to 0.01 through 100.
.TP
\fBpanes.activeBorder\fR (boolean; Lua \fBpanes.active_border\fR)
Paint the divider gap around the active pane in the theme's accent colour while the tab has splits. Read every frame.
.TP
\fBpanes.dividerThickness\fR (number; Lua \fBpanes.divider_thickness\fR)
Gap between split panes in logical pixels, scaled and rounded to whole device pixels and filled with the theme's border colour; 0 removes it, values above 32 are clamped. Read every frame.
.TP
\fBscrollback.limitBytes\fR (integer; Lua \fBscrollback.limit_bytes\fR)
Maximum raw history ring bytes per session, counted as (lines + rows) * columns * 12; 0 means no byte cap. Non\-zero values below 1048576 and negative values fall back to the default. The first of this and limitLines to be reached applies.
.TP
\fBscrollback.limitLines\fR (integer; Lua \fBscrollback.limit_lines\fR)
Maximum history lines kept per session; 0 keeps no history. Clamped to at most 1000000; negative values fall back to the default. The first of this and limitBytes to be reached applies.
.TP
\fBsearch.caseSensitive\fR (boolean; Lua \fBsearch.case_sensitive\fR)
Search overlay starts case\-sensitive. Alt+C toggles it while the overlay is open.
.TP
\fBsearch.regex\fR (boolean; Lua \fBsearch.regex\fR)
Search overlay starts in regular\-expression mode (.NET syntax; an invalid pattern is searched literally and marked). Alt+R toggles it while the overlay is open.
.TP
\fBsearch.wholeWord\fR (boolean; Lua \fBsearch.whole_word\fR)
Search overlay starts matching whole words only (neither end touches a letter, digit, or underscore). Alt+W toggles it while the overlay is open.
.TP
\fBselection.clearOnCopy\fR (boolean; Lua \fBselection.clear_on_copy\fR)
Clear the selection after the Copy action put it on the clipboard.
.TP
\fBselection.clearOnTyping\fR (boolean; Lua \fBselection.clear_on_typing\fR)
Clear the selection when typed text or a key is sent to the pane.
.TP
\fBselection.rectangleModifier\fR (string; Lua \fBselection.rectangle_modifier\fR)
Modifier that, held when a drag starts, makes a rectangular (block) selection; 'none' disables block selection. Ctrl and Shift also have click meanings (links, extend), which then lose to the block gesture. Unknown values mean alt. One of: alt, ctrl, shift, super, none.
.TP
\fBselection.wordChars\fR (string; Lua \fBselection.word_chars\fR)
Punctuation a double\-click keeps inside a word, besides letters, digits, combining marks, '_' and emoji clusters (CJK included). Other punctuation selects as runs of its own; an empty string keeps no punctuation.
.TP
\fBselectionColor\fR (string; Lua \fBselection_color\fR)
Selection highlight color as a hex string (for example #3385DB); the built\-in translucent blue when unset or invalid.
.TP
\fBshellIntegration\fR (string; Lua \fBshell_integration\fR)
Automatically inject Dotty's shell\-integration scripts (OSC 7 / OSC 133) into recognized interactive shells: 'detect' injects, 'none' never does; any other value is treated as none. An explicit command and the DOTTY_SHELL_INTEGRATION opt\-out are never overridden. One of: detect, none.
.TP
\fBtabBar.height\fR (number; Lua \fBtab_bar.height\fR)
Tab strip height.
.TP
\fBtabBar.show\fR (boolean; Lua \fBtab_bar.show\fR)
Show the tab bar.
.TP
\fBtabBar.style\fR (string; Lua \fBtab_bar.style\fR)
Tab bar style; the renderer currently uses one chrome style, so the stored value does not change the appearance. One of: Pill, Compact, Minimal.
.TP
\fBterm\fR (string; Lua \fBterm\fR)
TERM value for shells and commands Dotty starts: 'xterm\-256color', or a terminfo entry such as 'xterm\-dotty' (shipped in the packages). When the entry is not found in any terminfo directory (TERMINFO, ~/.terminfo, TERMINFO_DIRS, the system directories, or the bundled terminfo directory), xterm\-256color is used. XTGETTCAP TN reports the value actually used.
.TP
\fBtheme\fR (string; Lua \fBtheme\fR)
Built\-in or user theme name (user themes load from <config\-directory>/themes); the dark fallback when themeAuto is true. The DOTTY_THEME environment variable overrides it.
.TP
\fBthemeAuto\fR (boolean; Lua \fBtheme_auto\fR)
Follow the OS light/dark color scheme, selecting themeDark (or theme) or themeLight.
.TP
\fBthemeDark\fR (string; Lua \fBtheme_dark\fR)
Theme used when themeAuto is true and the OS reports a dark color scheme; falls back to theme when unset.
.TP
\fBthemeLight\fR (string; Lua \fBtheme_light\fR)
Theme used when themeAuto is true and the OS reports a light color scheme; LightPlus when unset.
.TP
\fBvt.checksumReportEnabled\fR (boolean; Lua \fBvt.checksum_report_enabled\fR)
Answer DECRQCRA (CSI Pi ; Pg ; Pt ; Pl ; Pb ; Pr * y) rectangular\-area checksum requests; off by default because the reply lets a program read back screen content. When false no reply is sent.
.TP
\fBvt.windowResizeAllowed\fR (boolean; Lua \fBvt.window_resize_allowed\fR)
Let applications resize the window with CSI 8 ; rows ; cols t (and CSI Ps t with Ps >= 24). Ignored with several tabs, split panes, or a maximized, fullscreen or minimized window.
.TP
\fBwindow.columns\fR (integer; Lua \fBwindow.columns\fR)
Initial grid width in cells; 0 uses 80. Read at startup.
.TP
\fBwindow.decorations\fR (string; Lua \fBwindow.decorations\fR)
Windows only: 'custom' draws the tab\-bar caption controls instead of the native title bar; other platforms always keep native decorations. One of: custom, native.
.TP
\fBwindow.floating\fR (boolean; Lua \fBwindow.floating\fR)
Keep the window above other windows (always on top).
.TP
\fBwindow.opacity\fR (number; Lua \fBwindow.opacity\fR)
Default\-background opacity 0\-1, multiplied by the theme opacity; text, chrome and images stay opaque. Going from 1 to below 1 needs a restart.
.TP
\fBwindow.padding.bottom\fR (number; Lua \fBwindow.padding.bottom\fR)
Bottom padding around the terminal content.
.TP
\fBwindow.padding.left\fR (number; Lua \fBwindow.padding.left\fR)
Left padding around the terminal content.
.TP
\fBwindow.padding.right\fR (number; Lua \fBwindow.padding.right\fR)
Right padding around the terminal content.
.TP
\fBwindow.padding.top\fR (number; Lua \fBwindow.padding.top\fR)
Top padding around the terminal content.
.TP
\fBwindow.rows\fR (integer; Lua \fBwindow.rows\fR)
Initial grid height in cells; 0 uses 24. Read at startup.
.TP
\fBwindow.startFullscreen\fR (boolean; Lua \fBwindow.start_fullscreen\fR)
Enter fullscreen when the window is first shown; wins over startMaximized. Read at startup.
.TP
\fBwindow.startMaximized\fR (boolean; Lua \fBwindow.start_maximized\fR)
Maximize the window when it is first shown. Read at startup.
.TP
\fBwindow.title\fR (string; Lua \fBwindow.title\fR)
Initial window title; the title then follows the active tab. Read at startup.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBDOTTY_CONFIG_HOME\fR
Overrides the complete configuration directory.
.TP
\fBDOTTY_THEME\fR
Overrides the configured theme.
.TP
\fBDOTTY_PTY_HELPER\fR
Path of the \fBpty\-helper\fR executable to use.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/dotty/config.json\fR
User configuration.
